Finally, my portfolio website is live! 🎉

I've been working on deeptanil.in, a portfolio that I wanted to feel a little different from the usual developer portfolio.

I decided to make it Minecraft themed, and there's actually a reason behind it.

I've loved Minecraft since I was around 10 years old. As I got older, that interest turned into experimenting with Minecraft servers, development, and other tech around the game.

So when I started building my own portfolio, using Minecraft as the theme just felt right.

I built the website to experiment and showcase my skills with 3D models, 3D text, smooth scrolling animations, interactive elements, and custom UI to bring the idea together.

It's not just a portfolio for me. It's also a project where I get to combine the things I enjoy most: technology, design, and building products.

There's still more I want to add, but I'm really happy with how it's turned out so far.

Take a look: deeptanil.in👀

